  "worked_solution": "The derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}\u2061x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{arsinh}\u20612}{2(1-{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{arsinh}\u20612}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{arsinh}\u20612}{2}\\,\\operatorname{artanh}\u2061x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
